<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  VirtualDriver verification scenario 08_overtake / overtake_slow_lead_on_two_lane_road

  vd-func:FUNC-056 (overtake maneuver) / req-vd-ad:REQ-AD-023 acceptance ladder
  step a-c ("遅い先行車を追い越して巡航速度へ戻る", the clean success case).
  Isolates the SAME-DIRECTION passing-lane path (design doc section 4: passing
  lane = the adjacent lane whose id is closer to 0) from the route-budget guard
  (section 2) by giving the guard a LARGE margin, so this scenario measures
  "does the overtake complete and return" without also stressing "does the
  guard correctly decline" (that is overtake_declined_before_route_branch's
  job) or "does the safety valve correctly abort" (overtake_aborted_for_route_
  branch's job).

  Road: resources/scenario_authoring/road_catalog/generated/
  straight_restricted_exit__l800_lanes2_exitm2.xodr (gen_straight_restricted_exit.py
  length=800 lanes=2 exit_lane=-2). Main road (id 0) is 800 m straight,
  2 lanes per direction; a junction (id 100) at its end forks into a THROUGH
  continuation (road 1, both lanes 1:1 - not used by this scenario) and an
  EXIT ramp (road 2, one lane) reachable from ONLY road 0 lane -2 (connecting
  road 101, laneLink "-2" -> "-1" - verified via the checker script's own
  parse_xodr output, not assumed). Ego therefore MUST end the run on lane -2,
  not -1 (the passing lane) - this is exactly the property that would be
  impossible to test on an ordinary symmetric multi-lane road (see this
  generator's own header comment / overtake_maneuver.md section 9-4).

  == distance-budget arithmetic (design doc sections 2-3; see the parent
  session's own report for the full derivation) ==
    v_pass = 20.0 m/s (EgoCruiseSpeed, Story-side step SpeedAction - see
             lane 11-11 note below for why NOT a linear ramp)
    v_lead = 8.0 m/s (SlowLeadSpeed)   =>  delta_v = 12.0 m/s
    g0 = 40.0 m (bumper-to-bumper gap at t=0: SlowLead's LanePosition s is
         ego_s + g0 + L_ego/2 + L_lead/2 = 30 + 40 + 5 = 75)
    L_ego = L_lead = 5.0 m (car_white / car_red BoundingBox length)
    g1 = lane_change_gap_min_m = 8.0 m (config, reused per design section 3)
    L_clear = g0 + g1 + L_ego + L_lead = 40 + 8 + 5 + 5 = 58.0 m
    t_pass  = L_clear / delta_v = 58.0 / 12.0 = 4.8333 s
              (<= overtake_max_pass_time_s = 10.0 -> trigger condition holds;
              delta_v_min = L_clear / 10.0 = 5.8 m/s, our delta_v=12.0 clears it)
    duration_max_s = resume_merge_duration_max_s = 6.0 (config)
    d_out = d_back = v_pass * duration_max_s = 20.0 * 6.0 = 120.0 m
    n_back = 1 (passing lane -1 is ONE hop from the target-lane band {-2} -
              design doc section 2-1)
    d_route = n_back * max(v_pass*lane_change_lead_time_s(6.0),
              lane_change_min_lead_distance_m(40.0)) + lane_change_reserve_
              distance_m(20.0) = 1*max(120.0,40.0)+20.0 = 140.0 m
    required = d_out + d_pass + d_back + d_route + lane_change_reserve_
               distance_m(20.0, outer)
             = 120.0 + (20.0*4.8333=96.667) + 120.0 + 140.0 + 20.0 = 496.667 m
    dist_to_connection at t=0 = road-0 length(800) - Ego s(30) = 770.0 m
    GUARD: required(496.667) <= dist_to_connection(770.0) - PASSES, with a
    273.33 m margin (deliberately large: SIGNAL_OUT/SIGNAL_BACK indicator-lead
    dwell time is spent still cruising at v_pass, so it does not need a
    SEPARATE distance allowance in this formula, but the margin is kept
    generous anyway since the exact runtime distance consumption during the
    lateral hops has not been measured against a real build - see the
    parent report's confidence notes).

  StopTrigger=50s: total path from Ego's start to a confirmably-on-the-exit-
  ramp point (road0 800-30=770 m to the junction, + connecting road 101's
  measured length 60.192 m, + 40 m into road 2) = 870.19 m; at a constant
  v_pass=20 m/s that is ~43.5 s. 50 s leaves a margin to observe the phase
  settle back to idle after the return-hop completes.

  Ego cruise speed is set via a STEP (not linear) SpeedActionDynamics in the
  Story (SimulationTimeCondition value="0.0"), per resources/xosc/verification/
  06_route_lane/lane_change_to_exit_ramp_at_constant_speed.xosc's convention
  (route_lane_batch.yaml's own notes record that a LINEAR ramp shrinks the
  measured indicator lead time via required_m outpacing the ego's closing
  speed while still accelerating - lane_change_initiation.md section 11-11).
  This scenario deliberately avoids that transient so v_pass is exactly the
  design doc's static v_pass from frame 1, matching this file's arithmetic.

  SlowLead carries no ObjectController (esmini's default lane-following
  behavior - constant SpeedAction, no Route needed), the same pattern
  resources/xosc/verification/06_route_lane/lane_change_to_exit_ramp_with_
  traffic.xosc uses for its own background vehicle.

  overtake_enabled / policy_lead_enabled are injected via this batch's
  "policies: [overtake, lead]" entry (resources/xosc/verification/
  overtake_batch.yaml) - not a static Property here, same mechanism the
  06_route_lane family uses for lane_change_initiation_enabled. "lead" (the
  IDM follow policy) is included so Ego's ACTUAL speed realistically slows to
  follow SlowLead if the overtake decision is delayed, rather than closing
  at full v_pass with no collision-avoidance response at all.
-->
<OpenSCENARIO>
   <FileHeader revMajor="1"
               revMinor="1"
               date="2026-08-04T00:00:00"
               description="VirtualDriver verification: overtake a slow lead vehicle on a 2-lane road and return to the exit-connected lane before the route branch"
               author="GT_esmini"/>
   <ParameterDeclarations>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="EgoCruiseSpeed" parameterType="double" value="20.0"/>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="SlowLeadSpeed" parameterType="double" value="8.0"/>
   </ParameterDeclarations>
   <CatalogLocations/>
   <RoadNetwork>
      <LogicFile filepath="../../../scenario_authoring/road_catalog/generated/straight_restricted_exit__l800_lanes2_exitm2.xodr"/>
   </RoadNetwork>
   <Entities>
      <ScenarioObject name="Ego">
         <Vehicle name="car_white" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_white.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="0"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
         <ObjectController>
            <Controller name="VirtualDriverController">
               <Properties>
                  <Property name="esminiController" value="VirtualDriverController"/>
               </Properties>
            </Controller>
         </ObjectController>
      </ScenarioObject>
      <ScenarioObject name="SlowLead">
         <Vehicle name="car_yellow" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_yellow.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="1"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
      </ScenarioObject>
   </Entities>
   <Storyboard>
      <Init>
         <Actions>
            <Private entityRef="Ego">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position>
                        <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="30"/>
                     </Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <RoutingAction>
                     <AssignRouteAction>
                        <Route name="ego_route" closed="false">
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="30"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <!--
                             Explicit connecting-road Waypoint (junction 100,
                             connection id=2, connecting road 101): required
                             so RoadManager::Route::AddWaypoint does not
                             silently truncate the route across the junction
                             (scripts/check_route_waypoints.py rule; verified
                             against this file with that checker, see the
                             parent report).
                           -->
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="101" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="30.1"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="2" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="40"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                        </Route>
                     </AssignRouteAction>
                  </RoutingAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <!--
                       Init-side SpeedAction. REQUIRED, and not redundant with the
                       Story-side one below. ControllerVirtualDriver::ResolveTargetSpeed()
                       only picks up a LONG_SPEED action while it is RUNNING; a
                       dynamicsShape="step" action can complete before the controller ever
                       observes it, leaving last_action_target_ pinned at its seed value
                       (object_->GetSpeed() at the first Step). Measured 2026-08-04 without
                       this action: ego.speed stayed 0.0 and ego.s stayed 30.000444 for the
                       whole 50 s run. Setting the speed here makes that seed the cruise
                       speed, so the ego is at v_pass from t=0 and the distance budget in
                       this file's header holds exactly (no acceleration ramp to subtract).
                     -->
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget>
                           <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoCruiseSpeed"/>
                        </SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <ControllerAction>
                     <ActivateControllerAction lateral="true" longitudinal="true"/>
                  </ControllerAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
            <Private entityRef="SlowLead">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position>
                        <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="75"/>
                     </Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget>
                           <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$SlowLeadSpeed"/>
                        </SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
         </Actions>
      </Init>
      <Story name="OvertakeStory">
         <Act name="OvertakeAct">
            <ManeuverGroup maximumExecutionCount="1" name="EgoSequence">
               <Actors selectTriggeringEntities="false">
                  <EntityRef entityRef="Ego"/>
               </Actors>
               <Maneuver name="CruiseManeuver">
                  <Event name="Cruise" priority="overwrite">
                     <Action name="CruiseAction">
                        <PrivateAction>
                           <LongitudinalAction>
                              <SpeedAction>
                                 <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                                 <SpeedActionTarget>
                                    <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoCruiseSpeed"/>
                                 </SpeedActionTarget>
                              </SpeedAction>
                           </LongitudinalAction>
                        </PrivateAction>
                     </Action>
                     <StartTrigger>
                        <ConditionGroup>
                           <Condition name="CruiseStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                              <ByValueCondition>
                                 <SimulationTimeCondition value="0.0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                              </ByValueCondition>
                           </Condition>
                        </ConditionGroup>
                     </StartTrigger>
                  </Event>
               </Maneuver>
            </ManeuverGroup>
            <StartTrigger>
               <ConditionGroup>
                  <Condition name="ActStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                     <ByValueCondition>
                        <SimulationTimeCondition value="0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                     </ByValueCondition>
                  </Condition>
               </ConditionGroup>
            </StartTrigger>
         </Act>
      </Story>
      <StopTrigger>
         <ConditionGroup>
            <Condition name="StopCondition" delay="0" conditionEdge="rising">
               <ByValueCondition>
                  <SimulationTimeCondition value="50" rule="greaterThan"/>
               </ByValueCondition>
            </Condition>
         </ConditionGroup>
      </StopTrigger>
   </Storyboard>
</OpenSCENARIO>
